{"labs": [{"stimuli": [{"id": 0, "type": "welcome", "contents": [{}], "template_override": 1, "_data": []}, {"id": 1, "template_override": 1, "type": "audio", "title": "", "contents": [{"value": {"audiosrc": "enpe7n5le01ob03re2aud01", "coverimg": "enpe7n5le01ob03re2img01.jpg", "images": [{"id": 0, "image": "enpe7n5le01ob03re2img01.jpg", "text": "I will talk today about OOP. You might want to know that OPP stands for object-oriented programming, and it is very useful in the programming area as it contributes to problem-solving procedures. You're going to have to know about all aspects related to this topic if you want to become an outstanding programmer, and for that, you ought to learn about 'classes'. Before creating any object, you'd better create its class first as it's basically the outline that the object will have once it's finished. Actually, it is of great help when you're going to create several objects as the same class will be implemented in each object saving you time; this way, you can include the particular characteristics for each one of those later.", "time": "100"}, {"id": 1, "image": "enpe7n5le01ob03re2img02.jpg", "text": "Now, you might want to know about the four different concepts that stem from OOP. First, you will have to learn about abstraction, in which the programmer only displays the most relevant information depending on the context. Now, you'd better bear in mind that encapsulation refers to a safety measure that protects data and restricts access to only authorized users. You also ought to know that with inheritance, we can create new classes from old ones, keeping the main characteristics of them. Finally, with polymorphism, we'll have several forms that share the same name. <br>", "time": "51000"}, {"id": 2, "image": "enpe7n5le01ob03re2img03.jpg", "text": "Other important elements to take into account are going to be 'methods' and 'functions'. A method delimits how an object behaves; for example, a method related to a \u2018dog' object ought to be barking or running. On the other hand, a function collects input to achieve a final result; for example, a function can calculate the price of a taxi by measuring the distance and time. Anyway, don't forget that I arrive tonight at your city. I'm speaking at the programmers' convention tomorrow at 6 pm!", "time": "93000"}]}, "type": "slideshow"}], "_data": []}], "id": 0, "type": "scholar", "exercises": [{"id": 0, "type": "WLC", "stimuli_ids": [0], "template_override": 1, "questions": [], "img_path": "", "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": "I can explain advanced concepts related to object-oriented programming. ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "I can talk about the importance of classes in object-oriented programming. ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "I can give examples about the concepts of method and function in object-oriented programming.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "Do you remember what the different uses of object-oriented programming are?", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": "What is the importance of object in programming languages? ", "type": "Free Header Item"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Welcome", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"content": {"allowed_attempts": 2, "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "try again", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time", "type": "text"}], "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "You have 2 tries", "type": "text"}, {"content": "you have 1 attempt left", "type": "text"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct"}, "type": "feedback"}, {"content": "Ask your partner:", "type": "free_header_text"}, {"content": "Important Aspects in OOP", "type": "free_type_text_area"}]}, {"id": 1, "type": "STI", "stimuli_ids": [1], "template_override": 1, "questions": [{"id": 0, "responses": [{"selected": 0, "id": 0, "correct": 0, "_data": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}]}, {"selected": 0, "id": 1, "correct": 1, "_data": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}]}], "_da